1
00:00:00,825 --> 00:00:02,325
(Penny:)What?

2
00:00:02,493 --> 00:00:05,783
Secret-keeping is a complicated endeavor.
One has to be concerned...

3
00:00:05,955 --> 00:00:10,125
(Sheldon:)...not only about what one says, but about
facial expressions, autonomic reflexes.

4
00:00:10,543 --> 00:00:11,873
(Sheldon:)When I try to deceive...

5
00:00:12,044 --> 00:00:16,714
(Sheldon:)...I myself have more nervous tics
than a Lyme disease research facility.

6
00:00:22,013 --> 00:00:23,053
(Sheldon:)It's a joke.

7
00:00:23,222 --> 00:00:27,022
It relies on the homonymic relationship
between tick, the bloodsucking arachnid...

8
00:00:27,185 --> 00:00:29,645
(Sheldon:)...and tic, the involuntary
muscular contraction.

9
00:00:29,812 --> 00:00:31,232
[CHUCKLES]

10
00:00:34,275 --> 00:00:35,445
(Sheldon:)I made it up myself.

11
00:00:38,279 --> 00:00:43,279
(Penny:)Okay, look, if Leonard finds out that I lied,
I will absolutely die of embarrassment.

12
00:00:43,451 --> 00:00:46,451
- Physiologically impossible.
- Oh, Sheldon, please.

13
00:00:46,621 --> 00:00:48,621
(Penny:)Look, I'm asking you as a friend.

14
00:00:49,999 --> 00:00:52,339
(Sheldon:)You're saying that friendship
contains within it...

15
00:00:52,502 --> 00:00:55,082
(Sheldon:)...an inherent obligation
to maintain confidences?

16
00:00:55,254 --> 00:00:58,674
- Well, yeah.
- Interesting.

17
00:00:59,217 --> 00:01:01,637
(Sheldon:)One more question.
Perhaps I should've led with this:

